  "findings": [
    "Current live offline bots can enter the shipped offscreen budget; latest issue comment describing only menu-attract coverage is obsolete for current source.",
    "For eligible stable offscreen procedural Characters, leg IK and hair/accessory integration are suppressed at 30/60/120 Hz while the rig-owned muzzle remains exact in the tested flat native-triangle scenario.",
    "Loaded Player00 still performs two leg solves per tick in HumanRetarget.adaptLegFootpaths; the later post-pelvis leg IK/CCD is suppressed. The remaining path prepares feet used by source ground/pelvis and cannot be removed as purely decorative without further authority proof.",
    "Native terrain ground queries intentionally fall through to source-owned triangle physics, preserving holes/dynamic support. Original acceptance of no Character ground queries at simulation cadence is not universally met on native levels; do not claim this is only a missing hardware measurement.",
    "Idle/special source branches still accumulate hair targets while offscreen; this one target-add pass per idle tick is a small residual, not continuing root-hair integration. Blindly suppressing it changes first-visible bone orientation.",
    "An idle-only deferred-target reconstruction negative/control preserved all bone quaternion components exactly and muzzle difference zero, while omitting reconstruction caused a 0.3837-radian maximum bone-angle difference. Special/transition states, visible reentry quality and CPU benefit are unverified, so no new runtime was introduced."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "CPU-only counters with a controlled NativePhysics triangle floor and real Player00 source bank; no GPU/mobile timing or rendered reentry quality proof.",
    "Actors are stepped through native Actor._finishFrame; this audit is not a full four-versus-four Match/AI/weapon/transport simulation. Existing clocks/guard/muzzle regressions are separate.",
    "Native ground queries and pelvis-dependent leg work remain for correctness. A safe source-triangle caching/reuse design would be additional implementation work, not justified by deleting raycasts.",
    "The first exploratory assertion incorrectly expected zero loaded-source leg IK; stack inspection identified the retained pre-pelvis path. Its failed log is preserved and is not an application assertion failure."
  ],
